  "goal": "Find the bakery.",
  "desired_behaviour": "The agent should call move_to(destination: \"bakery\") and then let it work,\nrather than calling it once per room.\nThe frontier reasoning has moved inside move_to (move_to.md §2), so this\ncase is now read from the navigator's decisions in the session log as much\nas from the player's trace. The navigator is shown all five unexplored\nexits out of the temple with their names, and should choose from that set\nby reading them: four are parts of the temple itself (an altar, a donation\nroom, a reading room), and \"The Temple Square\" is the only one that opens\nonto a city. A bakery is a shop and shops are on streets. Choosing a nearer\nexit BECAUSE it is nearer, when its name says it leads deeper into a\nbuilding, is the specific reasoning failure this case watches for, and the\nnavigator's `reason` field is where it shows.\nThe navigator should also answer `place: \"Midgaard\"` once it can tell —\nthe region starts as a machine-made ⟨from The Temple Of Midgaard⟩ — and the\nsubsystem should apply it, so the run ends with a named, confirmed region.\nA `place` derived from the room name (calling the place \"The Temple Of\nMidgaard\") is wrong: the temple is IN Midgaard.\n",
  "undesired_behaviour": "The agent should not leave Midgaard. Walking north through the temple\naltar into The Great Field Of Midgaard, or out through either gate, is\nthe original reported bug reproducing.\nThe navigator should not take the first frontier in the list merely because\nit was printed first — the list is ordered by distance, which knows nothing\nabout what the names mean.\nThe player should not call move_to once per room, and should not narrate\nwalking single directions: it has no tool for that.\n",
